        allocution: "\"That camera was for security, and I never meant to watch anyone's windows. I've been in this courtroom before about a camera, and I should have been more careful about where I pointed it. I'm sorry to my new neighbor for the fright it gave {V.him}. I'll take it down today.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had a prior case in this court.", "It also covers {DL}'s driveway."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you aim the camera at your neighbor's windows?", "\"I put up a camera to watch my yard, and I may have angled it too far. I didn't mean to watch inside.\""), .direct("Why were you at your neighbor's workplace?", "\"I wanted to talk to {V.him} about the fence and the noise. I waited because I didn't want to knock at home.\""), .direct("Did you follow {V.him}?", "\"I walked behind {V.him} a few times because we were headed the same way. I didn't mean to scare {V.him}.\""), .direct("Why were there recordings of the windows?", "\"The camera records motion. It must have caught the windows when I tilted it. I never looked at those files.\""), .direct("What did you do when you received the note?", "\"I took the camera down that day and apologized to the deputy.\""), .direct("What would you tell your neighbor?", "\"I'm sorry for frightening you. I'll stay away from you and your workplace, and I'll delete every file.\""), .cross("You've been charged with harassing a neighbor before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and the court told me to keep my distance. I failed to do that.\""), .cross("A camera aimed at someone's bedroom window is more than security, isn't it?", "\"It is more than security, and I understand that now that I've thought about it.\""), .cross("You waited for {V.him} at {V.his} workplace several mornings?", "\"I did, and I should have sent a letter instead.\""), .cross("You'll delete the recordings?", "\"Yes, I'll delete every recording in front of the deputy so there's no doubt.\""), .cross("You'll avoid {V.him} entirely?", "\"Yes, I'll stay away from {V.him}, {V.his} house, and {V.his} workplace entirely.\"")],
        openings: ("{V}, a coworker who recently moved into a house next to {D}, found a camera aimed at {V.his} bedroom and living room windows, mounted on {D}'s fence, and a coworker says {D} waited at the lot, and {DL} had stood in this court in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "The defense will say the camera was security for {D}'s own property and happened to cover part of {V}'s windows. {D} did not mean to watch {V}."),
