        role: "911 dispatcher",
        exam: [.direct("What is your job?", "\"I'm a 911 dispatcher, and I answer emergency calls and send deputies and ambulances.\""), .direct("What call did you receive?", "\"A caller said a gunman was walking through a mall, and then hung up before I could ask questions.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I sent deputies and alerted the mall security, and the mall locked down while officers searched every store.\""), .direct("How long did the lockdown last?", "\"About two hours, with hundreds of shoppers kept inside and several businesses forced to close.\""), .direct("What did the call record show?", "\"The call came from a prepaid phone that had been activated only that day.\""), .direct("What did the store camera show?", "\"{DL} buying a prepaid phone at a store the morning before the call, paying in cash.\""), .cross("The call was very short?", "\"Less than thirty seconds, and the caller didn't give a name.\""), .cross("The phone hasn't been found?", "\"No, it was turned off after the call.\""), .cross("{DL} bought the phone in {D.his} own name?", "\"No, but the camera shows {D.him} at the counter.\""), .cross("There was no gunman?", "\"None at all. The deputies searched every store and found no gunman and no weapon.\""), .cross("Nobody was hurt?", "\"No, though several people panicked and a woman fainted.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} called in a threat.", "A stolen phone."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry for the lockdown and for everyone in that mall who was scared. That prepaid phone was stolen from me, and I didn't make the call. I've been in this courtroom before, and I know my history makes me an easy name to put on it. I hope the real caller is found.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had a prior case in this court.", "{DL} reported it stolen later."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you make the call?", "\"No, I did not. The phone was stolen from me before that day, and I didn't make any call.\""), .direct("Why were you on camera buying a phone?", "\"I bought it for myself, and it was taken from my car that afternoon.\""), .direct("Did you report the theft?", "\"No. I should have, and I didn't, because I thought it was too small to bother with.\""), .direct("Where were you during the call?", "\"At work, in a plant a few miles away, and my supervisor can say so.\""), .direct("What did you tell the deputy?", "\"I told {OFF.him} the same thing, and I showed {OFF.him} the box from the phone.\""), .direct("What would you tell the shoppers and the mall?", "\"I'm sorry for what happened to you. I wasn't the caller, and I hope you find who was.\""), .cross("You've been charged with making a false report before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I know why you suspect me. I'm telling the truth this time.\""), .cross("You bought the phone the day before the call?", "\"I did, and that timing is bad luck for me.\""), .cross("You paid cash so it couldn't be traced?", "\"I paid cash because I was low on funds and had no card.\""), .cross("You'll let the court see your work records?", "\"Yes, and I'll sign a release for them.\""), .cross("You'll give the deputy your phone?", "\"Yes, right now, and I'll hand the deputy the phone and the box it came in.\"")],
        openings: ("A 911 dispatcher took a call from a person who said a gunman was walking through a mall and then hung up before the dispatcher could ask questions, forcing a lockdown, and a prepaid phone was traced to {D}, and a store camera shows {D} buy a phone, and this was not {DL}'s first time here, after {PRIOR} in {PRIORDATE}.", "The defense will say the phone was stolen from {D}, and {D} never made the call. A phone is not a person."),
        closings: ("The call record shows a prepaid phone, the store camera shows {D} buy it, and having faced {PRIOR} before, {DL} understood exactly what a call like that does to a mall.", "A stolen phone carries the owner's name but not the thief's voice. The State must prove {D}, and not whoever held the stolen phone, made the call to dispatch."),
        timeline: [(0, "2 p.m.: call."), (1, "Traced.")],
        identified: "Call Record",
        mood: .wantsConviction)

